  "query_preview": "../Tuesday through Thursday/...Active weather ensues\nheaded into mid week as the aforementioned system moves north\nacross the panhandle. An initial front is expected to move across\nthe panhandle Monday night into Tuesday morning bringing light to\nperiods of moderate rain. As mentioned in the short term\ndiscussion, communities across the northern panhandle could see a\nwintry mix at the onset of the front, but incoming cloud cover \ncould prevent temperatures from reaching low enough for frozen \nprecipitation to ensue. Precipitation chances along the north gulf\ncoast stay relatively low through Tuesday with this front \npotentially dying out or passing through just south of the area. \nModels are still split on the exact timing of the next front with \nthe Canadian and European models bringing rain up from the south \nTuesday morning, but the GFS has rain moving in Tuesday afternoon \nto evening. The GFS then indicates more of a break on Wednesday \nbefore a third front moves in, with the Canadian and the European \ngiving little to no respite between waves of rain. Rain continues \nthrough the day Thursday as well as another front moves across the\narea. \n\nThe strongest of these systems is expected to be the initial\nfront moving through on Monday into Tuesday, especially across the\nsouthern panhandle, bringing gale force winds up Clarence Strait.\nWinds are anticipated to remain elevated through the day Tuesday\nbefore diminishing Wednesday. The pressure gradient is likely to\nthen become the main driver of wind for the rest of the period as\na east/west pressure gradient sets up across the panhandle.",
